# #1409: the filter-rule and address-list push blocks' disabled, packets,
# bytes and dynamic, before (141f81e2, read off print as-value) and after
# (read with get by .id), on a real CHR 7.18.2, 2026-10-01.
# Each block once at the console with its /tool fetch swapped for :put,
# then the new pair saved as a script under the push policy (read,test)
# and run. Then: what get does for an entry that vanished mid-loop, and
# the payload size, old against new, on a 100-rule table.
# Fixture is probe data: documentation addresses plus the QEMU SLIRP
# gateway (10.0.2.2), so a rule's counter moves. No token: "tok".

